---
title: Per-Organization Enterprise SSO (OIDC & SAML)
---
%% An organization brings its own IdP. Registrations are resolved at request time from the
%% database, so onboarding a tenant is a row, not a redeploy.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SPA as Angular<br/>LoginComponent
    participant API as FederatedAuthController<br/>/oauth2
    participant REG as OrgAware…RegistrationRepository
    participant IDP as Organization's IdP<br/>Okta / Entra / Ping
    participant SH as Org success handler
    participant FLC as FederatedLoginCompletionService
    participant DB as MySQL

    rect rgba(107, 91, 255, 0.10)
    note over U, DB: Discovery — which IdP, if any, owns this email's domain?
    U->>SPA: Enter work email
    SPA->>API: GET /oauth2/org-sso-lookup?email=…
    API->>DB: Match the email DOMAIN to an organization
    alt domain has org SSO configured
        API-->>SPA: {found: true, orgId, protocol}
    else no match
        API-->>SPA: {found: false}
        note right of API: Says nothing about whether the<br/>ADDRESS exists — only whether its<br/>domain has SSO. Keyed on domain,<br/>not identity, precisely so it can't<br/>be used to enumerate accounts.
    end
    end

    alt protocol = OIDC
        SPA->>REG: Redirect /oauth2/authorization/org-{orgId}
        REG->>DB: Load this org's client id + secret
        REG->>REG: EncryptionUtil AES-256-GCM decrypt
        note right of REG: Client secrets are encrypted at rest.<br/>Key: ORG_IDP_SECRET_ENCRYPTION_KEY
    else protocol = SAML
        SPA->>REG: Redirect /saml2/authenticate/org-saml-{orgId}
        REG->>DB: Load this org's metadata URL
        REG->>IDP: Fetch + cache IdP metadata
    end

    REG->>IDP: Authentication request
    IDP->>U: Organization's own login (and its own MFA)
    U->>IDP: Authenticate
    IDP->>SH: Assertion / authorization code
    SH->>SH: Extract email + name<br/>(SAML: several candidate attributes, then NameID)

    SH->>FLC: complete(...)
    FLC->>DB: Resolve or create the user
    FLC->>DB: Auto-join the organization
    FLC-->>U: Redirect /oauth2/callback with our own JWTs

    note over U, DB: SAML shipped with code + unit tests but has never been run<br/>against a live IdP — see FUTURE-ENHANCEMENTS.md.
